{
  "_about": "Programs and paths a filter can't rest on, because a filter on them could hide an attacker. attacker_tools (including network-only tools a beacon could run through, and debuggers and memory readers used to dump secrets): never the pinned program, not even by exact command line. lolbins: the LOLBAS, GTFOBins and LOOBins catalogues (snapshot 2026-10-10), allowed only by exact command line. pinned_actions: event.action values (code injection, running from memory) filtered only with both the program and its parent pinned. internet_facing: browsers, mail, chat and office apps, where exploits land; their pinned_actions need more (agent/prompts/rules.md), and allow does not remove them. Override in safety.local.json (same keys; \"allow\" removes names) or with --allow NAME for one run.",
